WEBVTT

00:21.279 --> 00:22.750
(Ryeo Un)

00:24.109 --> 00:25.980
(Choi Hyun Wook)

00:28.019 --> 00:29.689
(Seol In Ah)

00:34.589 --> 00:36.729
(Shin Eun Soo)

00:44.170 --> 00:48.008
(Twinkling Watermelon)

00:48.009 --> 00:49.468
(Production sponsors)

00:49.469 --> 00:50.939
(Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism, KOCCA)

00:50.940 --> 00:51.979
(All people, organizations, locations, and incidents...)

00:51.980 --> 00:53.008
(in this drama are fictitious.)

00:53.009 --> 00:54.009
(Staff ensured child actors' safety in the filming of this drama.)

00:54.350 --> 00:56.709
(Episode 7)

01:04.219 --> 01:07.560
(Out of order)

01:21.009 --> 01:23.470
A patient coming through. Please step aside.

01:24.069 --> 01:25.279
Please step aside. Excuse us.

01:25.280 --> 01:26.940
We have a patient. Please move.

01:27.309 --> 01:28.380
Dad.

01:35.350 --> 01:36.390
Mom.

02:14.860 --> 02:17.030
(Incoming call)

02:23.569 --> 02:24.599
Hello?

02:24.600 --> 02:26.138
Hello, there.

02:26.139 --> 02:28.870
So are you having a pleasant trip?

02:29.239 --> 02:31.710
Come on. It was you?

02:31.880 --> 02:33.280
You scared me!

02:33.410 --> 02:35.409
You should have called me first if you were going to do this.

02:35.410 --> 02:37.310
- No, listen. I was...
- Whatever.

02:37.449 --> 02:39.078
I'm doing very well.

02:39.079 --> 02:41.049
Don't ever call me again. Got it?

02:41.190 --> 02:43.019
You must be having fun,

02:43.419 --> 02:44.889
living someone else's life.

02:51.799 --> 02:54.298
Hello?

02:54.299 --> 02:57.738
Are you there? Can you hear me?

02:57.739 --> 02:59.039
Anybody there?

02:59.739 --> 03:00.899
What's this? Did she hang up on me?

03:00.900 --> 03:02.139
Darn it.

03:02.239 --> 03:03.269
That's right.

03:03.440 --> 03:05.710
I'm living someone else's life.

03:06.280 --> 03:08.710
My name is On Eun Yu.

03:09.579 --> 03:11.078
You have probably guessed it.

03:11.079 --> 03:13.650
I'm Choi Se Gyeong's daughter from the 21st century.

03:14.489 --> 03:17.090
(New York, 2013)

03:22.660 --> 03:23.660
That's me.

03:24.500 --> 03:25.560
That's my mom.

03:26.130 --> 03:28.229
I know that we're very alike.

03:29.699 --> 03:31.940
Apparently, I resembled her even more as I grew up.

03:33.769 --> 03:36.410
I took after her so much that I was practically her clone.

03:36.569 --> 03:37.609
Anyway...

03:45.380 --> 03:48.350
Excellent. The girl is a genius.

03:53.690 --> 03:55.530
That's how I became my mother's precious gem.

03:57.030 --> 03:58.160
Was I happy?

03:59.130 --> 04:00.130
Not in the slightest.

04:04.030 --> 04:05.699
- Bravo!
- Bravo!

04:05.940 --> 04:08.769
As you know, a gem must shine all the time.

04:16.250 --> 04:19.419
The moment it loses its sparkle, its value will plummet.

04:45.679 --> 04:47.108
I was loved only briefly...

04:47.109 --> 04:48.309
when she needed to show off or put on a show.

04:49.249 --> 04:51.450
I was mostly locked up in my jewelry box.

05:06.400 --> 05:07.400
Hey.

05:14.510 --> 05:15.709
If my dad hadn't taken me...

05:15.710 --> 05:18.109
out of my mother's jewelry box from time to time,

05:18.710 --> 05:20.580
I would have died already.

05:21.580 --> 05:22.609
But...

05:23.309 --> 05:25.349
(Application on the Confirmation of Divorce by Consent)

05:25.350 --> 05:26.379
Eun Yu...

05:27.419 --> 05:28.820
is my daughter, so I'll raise her.

05:29.119 --> 05:30.450
I'm her father.

05:30.989 --> 05:32.919
If you want to raise her, you must stop drinking then.

05:35.629 --> 05:36.829
I already filled it out.

05:36.830 --> 05:38.129
I prayed to anyone who would listen.

05:38.460 --> 05:40.330
"Please make them stop fighting because of me."

05:45.840 --> 05:48.939
"Help me not regret that I was born." That's what I prayed.

05:49.210 --> 05:51.378
(Condolences)

05:51.379 --> 05:52.639
(Viva Music)

05:52.640 --> 05:54.179
Whose house is this?

05:55.179 --> 05:56.379
This was my father's house.

05:56.679 --> 05:58.479
But Grandpa lives in the US.

05:58.919 --> 06:00.520
Not him.

06:00.950 --> 06:02.350
He was your real grandpa.

06:03.320 --> 06:05.559
Grandpa in the US isn't my grandpa?

06:06.260 --> 06:07.289
No.

06:08.289 --> 06:11.160
I have two fathers. Jealous, are you?

06:12.160 --> 06:14.729
No. I only need one dad.

06:17.700 --> 06:18.770
You know,

06:19.840 --> 06:23.669
ever since I was a kid, I wanted my own family.

06:24.510 --> 06:26.379
A family that wasn't complicated to explain.

06:27.239 --> 06:29.979
A family I didn't have to worry about or be scared...

06:31.010 --> 06:32.820
of being abandoned by. A real family like that.

06:34.590 --> 06:37.090
You're my only family now.

06:37.320 --> 06:38.960
Dad isn't your real family?

06:42.059 --> 06:43.890
You'll stay by my side, right?

06:44.390 --> 06:46.499
You won't abandon me or leave me, right?

06:53.340 --> 06:54.340
I regretted it.

06:55.109 --> 06:58.039
I shouldn't have made that promise to her that day.

07:00.640 --> 07:03.978
(Viva Music)

07:03.979 --> 07:05.720
Like the change of the seasons,

07:05.979 --> 07:07.749
the relationship between my dad and my mother...

07:07.850 --> 07:09.249
cycled through hot and cold.

07:10.489 --> 07:12.058
They went through the cycle...

07:12.059 --> 07:13.619
of living together and getting separated like an annual event.

07:14.520 --> 07:17.659
In the end, the year I turned 18,

07:17.660 --> 07:18.859
they got a divorce.

07:19.900 --> 07:23.669
(6 years later)

07:31.410 --> 07:34.010
This is our home now. We'll live here, just the two of us.

07:35.749 --> 07:37.450
Just focus on studying music.

07:37.609 --> 07:38.749
You understand what I'm saying, right?

08:03.340 --> 08:05.809
Did she gain weight? She looks like she gained weight.

08:05.939 --> 08:07.879
Girls lose weight in college.

08:08.010 --> 08:09.978
It's normal for girls to gain weight until they finish high school.

08:09.979 --> 08:12.780
Ma'am, can you loosen up the waist a bit more?

08:12.879 --> 08:14.248
It will be uncomfortable when I perform.

08:14.249 --> 08:15.450
No. Leave it as it is.

08:16.489 --> 08:17.720
She'll lose weight pretty soon.

08:21.789 --> 08:22.830
Choi Se Gyeong?

08:26.299 --> 08:27.660
It's me.

08:27.929 --> 08:29.530
Yoon Sang A from Seowon Arts High School.

08:30.570 --> 08:32.600
The daughter of Jinsung Musical Instruments' chairman.

08:34.439 --> 08:36.169
I did hear that you were back in Korea.

08:36.609 --> 08:38.039
So it was true.

08:40.580 --> 08:43.150
No way. Is she your daughter?

08:43.580 --> 08:44.780
Hello.

08:45.879 --> 08:48.690
She's a carbon copy of you in high school.

08:50.220 --> 08:51.489
It's nice to see you.

08:51.960 --> 08:54.259
But what a pity. I have an appointment coming up soon.

08:55.529 --> 08:56.859
I heard about your news.

08:57.330 --> 08:58.529
You got divorced.

08:59.560 --> 09:01.129
I was a bit shocked.

09:01.159 --> 09:02.170
Darn it.

09:02.470 --> 09:04.739
The timer on the time bomb started to tick away.

09:04.840 --> 09:06.099
You and Ji Hwan...

09:06.100 --> 09:09.070
were the last couple I expected to see getting a divorce.

09:09.139 --> 09:10.908
- Three.
- I get it, though.

09:10.909 --> 09:13.080
It was even more shocking when you got married.

09:13.340 --> 09:15.810
I thought you would continue your career as a cellist.

09:16.609 --> 09:18.219
- Two.
- You were notably impressive...

09:18.220 --> 09:19.679
when you were in high school. You know?

09:19.680 --> 09:22.488
You were talented, beautiful,

09:22.489 --> 09:23.920
and popular too.

09:24.859 --> 09:27.919
Boys from other high schools worshipped you like some deity.

09:27.920 --> 09:29.930
They called you the Queen of Cello.

09:31.659 --> 09:32.700
One.

09:46.080 --> 09:47.608
I'm serious.

09:47.609 --> 09:50.409
A boy formed a band just for me.

09:50.909 --> 09:53.779
He said he would put on a show at the festival just for me.

09:54.479 --> 09:57.219
Right. Talking about bands brings back this memory.

09:57.220 --> 09:59.560
Did I tell you my first love was in a band?

10:01.560 --> 10:03.359
You see, my first love...

10:03.659 --> 10:05.930
was nothing like your father.

10:08.830 --> 10:12.540
He was bright like sunshine, cheerful, and manly.

10:14.170 --> 10:15.638
He seemed indifferent and cold from time to time,

10:15.639 --> 10:17.009
but he was kind.

10:17.909 --> 10:20.339
He was sometimes sensitive and meticulous.

10:20.340 --> 10:21.340
But he had a positive attitude.

10:21.341 --> 10:23.710
You should have married your first love.

10:24.950 --> 10:26.580
I wouldn't have been born then.

10:27.619 --> 10:28.619
What?

10:29.590 --> 10:31.320
Why don't I finish Part Two of your story?

10:32.359 --> 10:34.889
"If only I didn't marry your father..."

10:35.190 --> 10:37.330
"If only you weren't born, I would have had..."

10:37.489 --> 10:38.858
"a fantastic career as a cellist..."

10:38.859 --> 10:40.430
"and explored the world."

10:41.029 --> 10:43.069
"I wouldn't have lived as a boring woman..."

10:43.070 --> 10:45.300
"who clung on to her husband and obsessed over her daughter."

10:47.269 --> 10:49.309
Eun Yu. What I said...

10:49.310 --> 10:50.639
It was the liquor talking?

10:51.210 --> 10:52.779
You're never going to drink again?

10:53.109 --> 10:55.180
Do you expect me to fall for that promise again?

10:55.749 --> 10:57.978
Did you think I had a choice about being born?

10:57.979 --> 10:59.019
I...

10:59.580 --> 11:01.889
didn't get to choose to have you as my mother when I was born.

11:03.950 --> 11:05.090
Come on.

11:15.170 --> 11:16.600
What do you think you're doing?

11:16.700 --> 11:17.930
I'm going to live with Dad.

11:18.369 --> 11:19.699
I'm scared that...

11:19.700 --> 11:21.299
I might turn into you if I keep living with you.

11:21.300 --> 11:23.339
That's why I told you to focus only on music.

11:23.340 --> 11:24.368
So you won't turn into me!

11:24.369 --> 11:25.940
Stop giving me these excuses!

11:26.139 --> 11:28.108
Don't use me.

11:28.109 --> 11:30.680
Why must I be a tool for redeeming your failed life?

11:30.909 --> 11:32.050
I can't talk to you when you're like this.

11:32.920 --> 11:34.420
Talking was the last thing we ever did.

11:34.649 --> 11:36.289
You were always busy telling me what was on your mind.

11:36.290 --> 11:37.919
Whenever I talked, you treated me like some dog barking.

11:37.920 --> 11:40.060
Is that why you put on an act that you lost your hearing?

11:40.220 --> 11:42.559
Is that why you gave up that easily?

11:42.560 --> 11:44.128
Just to rebel against me?

11:44.129 --> 11:45.759
This is why I hate you.

11:46.499 --> 11:48.700
It's so easy for you to spit out these hurtful words.

11:48.970 --> 11:51.800
Sometimes, you act like a sociopath.

11:52.340 --> 11:54.700
Dad left because he was sick of this side of you. You know?

11:58.070 --> 11:59.239
How awful you are.

12:00.139 --> 12:03.180
You're just like your dad.

12:03.850 --> 12:04.879
You're right.

12:05.420 --> 12:07.050
I always got along with Dad much better than with you.

12:20.729 --> 12:22.800
That was the last day I spent with my mom,

12:26.139 --> 12:28.040
and it was the beginning of a long trip.

12:38.749 --> 12:41.050
(Incheon to JFK)

12:51.600 --> 12:52.759
Hello.

12:53.300 --> 12:54.330
Who are you?

12:54.600 --> 12:57.469
I'm sorry. But isn't this Dr. On's house?

12:57.470 --> 12:58.869
Yes. But who...

12:59.499 --> 13:01.840
I see. You're Dr. On's daughter.

13:02.670 --> 13:04.669
- Honey.
- "Honey?"

13:04.670 --> 13:06.680
Honey, come quick. Your daughter's here.

13:07.940 --> 13:10.350
He's on the second floor, so he can't hear us.

13:10.450 --> 13:11.580
Come in, sweetie.

13:12.519 --> 13:13.519
Honey.

13:22.159 --> 13:23.190
(Dad)

13:24.889 --> 13:25.999
(Dad)

13:31.970 --> 13:32.998
Darn it.

13:32.999 --> 13:33.999
(Mom)

13:42.109 --> 13:43.310
Dang, mama.

13:43.580 --> 13:45.079
- Where are you going?
- Sorry.

13:45.080 --> 13:47.519
- Do you want to hang out with us?
- Sorry.

13:51.220 --> 13:52.220
Oh, shoot.

13:57.090 --> 14:00.060
They should've married other people if they were going to do this.

14:01.430 --> 14:03.430
They shouldn't have had me then.

14:04.970 --> 14:07.269
They didn't even ask me what I wanted.

14:08.170 --> 14:10.470
I had no choice in my birth.

14:11.040 --> 14:13.108
It's not like they're going to live my life for me.

14:13.109 --> 14:15.050
What is this?

15:52.739 --> 15:54.509
- Welcome.
- Gosh, you startled me!

15:56.710 --> 15:58.649
I'm the master of this store.

15:58.879 --> 16:01.220
It must not have been easy to find this store.

16:01.350 --> 16:02.550
How did you find this place?

16:03.350 --> 16:06.759
No, you turned on the light for the sign just now.

16:07.989 --> 16:09.259
Yes. I did that, didn't I?

16:11.229 --> 16:13.259
Would you like a warm cup of tea?

16:13.399 --> 16:15.268
No, I'm good with tea.

16:15.269 --> 16:17.670
Do you buy used cellos?

16:17.830 --> 16:18.869
I want to sell it.

16:24.739 --> 16:26.379
Are you sure you want to sell this?

16:27.109 --> 16:29.249
I can tell you treated this cello with a lot of care.

16:30.379 --> 16:31.850
I don't need it anymore.

16:32.680 --> 16:34.180
I'm going to die soon.

16:34.379 --> 16:35.449
Oh, no.

16:35.450 --> 16:37.920
You're still very young. What made you become suicidal?

16:40.759 --> 16:43.489
Carrying that huge cello on my back...

16:43.690 --> 16:45.460
is way too heavy.

16:47.700 --> 16:49.028
But the cello doesn't seem...

16:49.029 --> 16:50.899
heavy enough to make someone suicidal.

16:52.700 --> 16:54.670
You can't probably see her,

16:54.869 --> 16:57.609
- but my mom is on that cello.
- Oh, my.

16:58.739 --> 17:01.079
Dad used to bring her down from the cello once in a while.

17:01.080 --> 17:02.580
But he's not interested in doing that anymore.

17:03.050 --> 17:05.080
So I think I'm ready to end my life.

17:05.350 --> 17:07.619
Your parents will be very sad.

17:07.749 --> 17:09.118
People say children fulfill a lifetime of duty...

17:09.119 --> 17:10.689
when they hit the age of three.

17:10.690 --> 17:12.320
It's not a bad deal for everyone.

17:12.859 --> 17:15.488
I'll have fun with the money from selling the cello.

17:15.489 --> 17:16.560
Then I'll die.

17:19.459 --> 17:20.530
Great!

17:20.929 --> 17:24.669
I will give you a very good price just for you.

17:28.169 --> 17:29.209
Gosh.

17:32.409 --> 17:33.639
Are you sure you're giving me a good price?

17:33.679 --> 17:35.280
I only see one-dollar bills.

17:36.409 --> 17:38.549
This will come in handy more than you think.

17:38.550 --> 17:39.649
Did you know?

17:40.080 --> 17:41.779
The design of one-dollar bills...

17:41.780 --> 17:44.419
has never changed unlike other bills.

17:49.790 --> 17:51.260
Here. Take this...

17:51.459 --> 17:54.599
in case you want to get your cello back.

17:54.600 --> 17:56.129
That will never happen.

17:57.969 --> 18:00.669
Take it just in case.

18:01.199 --> 18:02.209
Okay.

18:05.709 --> 18:07.939
Why don't you go on a trip before you die?

18:09.850 --> 18:11.879
I mean, it will be a special trip.

18:15.719 --> 18:16.719
Sounds good.

18:17.219 --> 18:19.760
It'll give me time to think about my suicidal plan. I'll do that.

18:20.990 --> 18:23.359
Thank you for the tea.

18:26.560 --> 18:28.359
Watch your way out.

18:29.629 --> 18:30.699
Okay.

18:31.969 --> 18:34.439
I hope you have a pleasant trip.

18:54.020 --> 18:55.060
What?

18:56.760 --> 18:57.829
(Entrance)

18:57.830 --> 18:58.929
What's this?

18:59.129 --> 19:00.458
This is an airport.

19:00.459 --> 19:01.969
(International Arrivals)

19:02.230 --> 19:03.300
An airport in Korea at that.

19:07.270 --> 19:08.570
(Who paged me?)

19:11.609 --> 19:12.609
What?

19:18.580 --> 19:20.280
"Year 1995?"

19:22.020 --> 19:24.189
Why don't you go on a trip before you die?

19:24.990 --> 19:26.820
I mean, it will be a special trip.

19:27.919 --> 19:30.060
And it was time travel?

19:30.659 --> 19:31.689
My gosh.

19:32.830 --> 19:33.859
Se Gyeong.

19:33.929 --> 19:35.770
Aren't you Se Gyeong?

19:36.129 --> 19:38.800
You are, right? I'm Kim Min Ji.

19:38.969 --> 19:41.469
We were classmates in sixth grade at Lala Elementary School.

19:42.209 --> 19:45.070
- Oh, yes. Min Ji.
- Yes, that's me.

19:45.139 --> 19:48.310
I heard you had left Korea to study abroad a few days ago.

19:48.480 --> 19:49.480
Did you not?

19:49.580 --> 19:51.279
- Abroad?
- Yes.

19:51.280 --> 19:52.280
Wait.

19:52.379 --> 19:54.780
So it's around when Mom just left Korea to study abroad.

19:55.119 --> 19:56.320
If so...

20:07.730 --> 20:09.969
It means this house will be empty for a while.

20:13.040 --> 20:16.168
So did you give up on dying now?

20:16.169 --> 20:17.438
(Daehan Telecommunication)

20:17.439 --> 20:19.209
Of course, I didn't.

20:19.280 --> 20:23.310
You just said you were doing well, didn't you?

20:23.480 --> 20:25.149
I am doing well.

20:25.750 --> 20:29.119
Because I found the most peaceful and fun way to take my own life.

20:29.490 --> 20:31.689
Gosh, can I ask what it is?

20:32.919 --> 20:35.118
It's not scary or painful.

20:35.119 --> 20:37.089
I won't have to bother anyone.

20:37.090 --> 20:39.830
And I will go out of existence very naturally.

20:40.699 --> 20:42.929
The suspense is killing me. Can you tell me more?

20:43.000 --> 20:45.300
I'm going to find my mom's first love so that they can stay together.

20:45.800 --> 20:48.168
Then she won't marry my dad.

20:48.169 --> 20:50.138
And I won't be born,

20:50.139 --> 20:52.540
which means I won't have to try hard to kill myself.

20:53.040 --> 20:54.840
Oh, my gosh.

20:55.310 --> 20:56.780
That's very creative.

20:56.879 --> 20:59.148
And my mom will be happier than she is now.

20:59.149 --> 21:01.280
Because she'll be with her first love as she wished.

21:02.219 --> 21:05.149
It's the most reasonable and elegant way to take my own life.

21:05.250 --> 21:06.820
Gosh, she's smart.

21:07.219 --> 21:09.289
That's very true.

21:09.290 --> 21:11.489
But how are you going to find her first love?

21:11.490 --> 21:13.359
- I already did.
- Oh, my gosh.

21:13.929 --> 21:16.230
Gosh, you're fast.

21:18.770 --> 21:21.669
But are you sure that it's him?

21:23.909 --> 21:27.040
Well... Are you saying that he isn't?

21:27.740 --> 21:28.750
I'm not sure.

21:29.449 --> 21:30.580
What do you think?

21:31.350 --> 21:32.350
Then...

21:33.449 --> 21:35.219
I'll get back to you in good time.

21:36.189 --> 21:38.049
Viva la vida.

21:38.050 --> 21:39.820
Hold on. Mister.

21:39.919 --> 21:41.389
Darn it. Hello?

21:42.020 --> 21:43.030
Hello?

21:51.969 --> 21:53.600
Does it mean that Mom's first love...

21:54.600 --> 21:56.469
might not be Yi Chan?

21:58.240 --> 22:00.010
Then who on earth is it?

22:22.629 --> 22:23.668
He's a patient with an electric shock.

22:23.669 --> 22:25.330
He was in a semi-coma on the way.

22:25.500 --> 22:26.868
His blood pressure has been decreasing.

22:26.869 --> 22:28.499
His pulse rate is less than 30 beats per minute,

22:28.500 --> 22:29.540
developing bradycardia.

22:29.939 --> 22:32.438
- Give him epinephrine right now.
- Yes, sir.

22:32.439 --> 22:34.208
And prepare the intubation set immediately.

22:34.209 --> 22:35.240
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

22:37.080 --> 22:38.108
He's in cardiac arrest.

22:38.109 --> 22:40.218
Do CPR. Hurry up and get the defibrillator.

22:40.219 --> 22:41.249
- Hurry up.
- Coming, sir.

22:41.250 --> 22:42.419
Charge 200 joules.

22:43.149 --> 22:44.290
Charge 200 joules. It's on.

22:44.389 --> 22:46.059
Please step back, everyone.

22:46.060 --> 22:47.520
Ready. Shoot.

22:49.230 --> 22:51.490
Mom. Dad.

22:52.959 --> 22:54.359
I want to go home.

22:57.330 --> 22:58.770
Please come and take me.

23:00.040 --> 23:01.070
Please.

23:07.109 --> 23:08.139
Are you okay?

23:12.449 --> 23:13.520
Oh, gosh.

23:13.820 --> 23:15.179
You're in a hospital.

23:15.449 --> 23:17.020
Hold on.

23:28.830 --> 23:31.369
You're in a hospital. You collapsed.

23:32.070 --> 23:33.070
Do you remember?

23:36.909 --> 23:39.139
What's the matter? Are you all right?

23:43.679 --> 23:44.850
It seems you remember.

23:45.379 --> 23:46.449
It's a relief.

23:46.949 --> 23:48.320
Just a second.

24:02.669 --> 24:04.000
I'm sorry I got mad at you last time.

24:04.570 --> 24:05.869
I'm sorry for the harsh words.

24:06.600 --> 24:08.740
I didn't know that you couldn't hear.

24:11.369 --> 24:12.408
I'm sorry.

24:12.409 --> 24:13.939
Don't be mistaken, Yoon Chung Ah.

24:14.409 --> 24:16.510
He's not being kind. He's pitying me.

24:17.149 --> 24:19.350
Do you think he would've been this kind...

24:19.480 --> 24:21.149
if I hadn't lost hearing?

24:21.350 --> 24:23.419
No, you can't.

24:23.949 --> 24:25.149
Don't move.

24:26.560 --> 24:27.590
You should lie down. That's what they said.

24:28.459 --> 24:30.959
They said you needed a rest.

24:31.230 --> 24:33.698
Excuse me. Can you come for a moment?

24:33.699 --> 24:34.760
Sure.

24:35.199 --> 24:37.199
I'll be back soon.

24:46.879 --> 24:48.638
(Hospital Discharge Form)

24:48.639 --> 24:50.810
(Relationship)

24:56.050 --> 24:57.689
(Friend)

24:58.719 --> 24:59.719
Here it is.

25:00.790 --> 25:03.459
Go to the reception to get a prescription for the patient.

25:03.659 --> 25:05.799
Make sure to stop by the pharmacy in the basement...

25:05.800 --> 25:06.928
to get the medication before leaving the hospital.

25:06.929 --> 25:09.270
All right. Thank you. Have a good day.

25:11.100 --> 25:12.129
My gosh.

25:23.449 --> 25:25.350
The invitation I gave you at that time.

25:26.219 --> 25:27.949
It was what Se Gyeong had given to me.

25:29.090 --> 25:32.119
I didn't know that she had put a letter in it.

25:33.020 --> 25:36.689
I'm asking why you screwed me up with this fake letter.

25:40.560 --> 25:42.330
I might not see you ever again,

25:42.730 --> 25:44.129
but I wanted to clarify the misunderstanding.

25:44.899 --> 25:46.540
Thank you for taking me to the hospital.

25:49.770 --> 25:50.770
(Yeonnam Hospital)

25:58.980 --> 26:00.280
(Please give me a chance to apologize.)

26:00.649 --> 26:01.980
Please give me a chance to apologize.

26:04.189 --> 26:05.219
Don't.

26:06.689 --> 26:07.820
I'm sorry that I misunderstood you.

26:10.830 --> 26:11.889
I'm really sorry.

26:12.659 --> 26:14.359
Don't keep apologizing like that.

26:15.300 --> 26:16.330
Aren't you hungry?

26:17.369 --> 26:18.570
Do you want to grab something?

26:19.270 --> 26:20.740
You need to eat to take your medication.

26:21.070 --> 26:22.469
Don't be so kind.

26:23.570 --> 26:24.669
You don't know.

26:25.240 --> 26:27.609
That too much kindness can hurt someone.

26:29.649 --> 26:31.679
Why? You can't forgive me?

26:31.949 --> 26:33.280
Do you think you'll never forgive me?

26:33.679 --> 26:36.790
How about you think about it while eating first?

26:37.149 --> 26:38.189
Aren't you hungry?

26:44.990 --> 26:46.199
I'm not hungry.

26:55.639 --> 26:56.939
You are hungry.

26:59.010 --> 27:02.139
No. I'm sorry. It's because I'm hungry.

27:02.310 --> 27:03.609
It's because I'm hungry.

27:04.580 --> 27:07.480
I paid the hospital bills.

27:08.179 --> 27:09.750
You pay for the meal.

27:28.469 --> 27:31.669
(On-the-spot Tteokbokki)

27:55.760 --> 27:57.429
Did you come to see me that day?

27:57.869 --> 27:59.770
Did you need my help?

28:00.800 --> 28:01.840
Help?

28:04.869 --> 28:06.409
Give me an SOS when you need help.

28:07.540 --> 28:09.179
I'll go with the guys who study sports in college.

28:15.219 --> 28:16.320
I'm relieved if it wasn't the case.

28:24.990 --> 28:26.600
(Did you come to see me that day?)

28:27.300 --> 28:28.300
Right.

28:29.800 --> 28:31.629
This is my fax number.

28:32.000 --> 28:35.199
If something happens, fax me at this number.

28:37.169 --> 28:39.810
If it's an emergency,

28:41.280 --> 28:43.178
page me first.

28:43.179 --> 28:45.310
Send "8282" or "505."

28:46.149 --> 28:47.320
Then I'll check right away.

28:48.050 --> 28:49.119
Okay?

28:57.560 --> 28:58.629
My heart...

28:59.560 --> 29:02.030
is fluttering again.

29:16.179 --> 29:19.320
Oh, do you want to part ways here?

29:20.649 --> 29:22.550
Will you be all right though?

29:24.419 --> 29:25.490
I mean, can you...

29:26.260 --> 29:29.020
go home by yourself?

29:32.030 --> 29:33.030
Right.

29:33.399 --> 29:36.969
I shouldn't insist on going to your place just because you aren't well.

29:38.000 --> 29:39.069
All right, then.

29:39.070 --> 29:42.570
Make sure you eat a lot.

29:43.139 --> 29:45.369
And don't forget...

29:46.780 --> 29:49.010
to take your medicine after each meal.

29:49.109 --> 29:51.050
I hope you recover soon...

29:51.879 --> 29:55.449
and become super healthy again.

29:59.859 --> 30:00.959
You smiled for the first time.

30:04.030 --> 30:06.699
Oh, it's nothing. Get home safely, then.

30:12.669 --> 30:15.070
Dad, you're supposed to be in love with Yoon Chung Ah!

30:15.270 --> 30:16.969
Wait, hold on.

30:17.369 --> 30:18.669
Do you know Ha Eun Gyeol?

30:19.280 --> 30:21.240
Oh, sorry. One moment.

30:29.550 --> 30:30.689
I see.

30:32.889 --> 30:34.159
That's right.

30:34.689 --> 30:36.530
We had a meal together,

30:37.060 --> 30:38.290
so we're friends now.

30:39.459 --> 30:41.699
Yoon Chung Ah.

30:47.639 --> 30:49.040
Tornado!

30:50.240 --> 30:51.639
(Yoon Chung Ah)

30:54.980 --> 30:57.609
He called my name.

31:22.500 --> 31:23.770
He called...

31:24.939 --> 31:26.109
my name.

31:36.550 --> 31:38.149
(This is my fax number.)

32:02.850 --> 32:04.179
(Snail Guesthouse)

32:05.350 --> 32:07.520
Hey, Ha Eun Gyeol!

32:10.350 --> 32:12.050
You mentioned someone named Yoon Chung Ah.

32:13.459 --> 32:14.959
Why am I supposed to be in love with...

32:23.000 --> 32:24.629
He didn't come home again? What's with this guy?

32:33.909 --> 32:34.980
My gosh.

32:36.280 --> 32:38.909
The patient in the VIP room is gone.

32:46.459 --> 32:48.388
(Who is the bandsman Mom loved?)

32:48.389 --> 32:51.260
If it's not Ha Yi Chan, who could it be?

32:52.330 --> 32:54.129
Gosh, I need some clues.

32:54.699 --> 32:56.629
Some telltale clues.

32:58.070 --> 32:59.839
My first love was...

32:59.840 --> 33:02.739
bright like sunshine and cheerful.

33:02.740 --> 33:04.309
He seemed like a tough guy,

33:04.310 --> 33:06.069
but he always liked me and no one else.

33:06.070 --> 33:07.079
(A hopeless slacker)

33:07.080 --> 33:09.010
He seemed indifferent and cold from time to time,

33:09.580 --> 33:11.479
but he was kind.

33:11.480 --> 33:12.749
(A hopeless slacker)

33:12.750 --> 33:14.749
He was sometimes sensitive,

33:14.750 --> 33:16.389
but he had a positive attitude.

33:17.719 --> 33:18.888
Darn it.

33:18.889 --> 33:21.118
Was her first love an AI robot or something?

33:21.119 --> 33:22.359
(Lee Si Guk, Ha Yi Chan, Ha Eun Gyeol, Kang Hyun Yul, No Se Bum)

33:26.629 --> 33:29.230
Oh, that's right. He was very good at eating spicy food.

33:30.699 --> 33:32.369
I couldn't handle spicy food at all.

33:33.070 --> 33:36.770
Once, I saw him eat something as if it wasn't spicy at all,

33:36.869 --> 33:38.770
so I stole a bite.

33:40.609 --> 33:43.648
My mouth and throat were on fire.

33:43.649 --> 33:45.050
No joke.

33:46.649 --> 33:48.649
I nearly ended up in the ER that day.

33:52.350 --> 33:53.389
My gosh.

33:54.159 --> 33:56.889
Eureka. It'll help me find out who he is, like a litmus test.

33:57.030 --> 33:59.230
I'll use this information to check.

34:00.859 --> 34:02.760
Hey, bro. It's me, Se Gyeong.

34:02.969 --> 34:05.829
I want to give you the photos from the amusement park.

34:05.830 --> 34:06.899
Can we meet?

34:07.969 --> 34:09.340
My gosh!

34:10.369 --> 34:11.708
Oh, my.

34:11.709 --> 34:13.340
She'll be hurt.

34:13.980 --> 34:15.480
I'm not easy.

34:25.350 --> 34:26.718
(It's very spicy.)

34:26.719 --> 34:27.989
(If you'd like it less spicy, let us know when ordering.)

34:30.529 --> 34:31.529
All right.

34:32.690 --> 34:34.330
(Civilian Government by President Kim Young Sam)

34:38.469 --> 34:39.540
Hi, Se Gyeong.

34:47.739 --> 34:48.778
What is he, a zombie?

34:48.779 --> 34:50.650
You seem to like bands.

34:51.279 --> 34:53.650
What do you say? Do you like my style?

34:53.880 --> 34:54.979
Of course, I don't.

34:54.980 --> 34:57.589
My gosh. Yes, you look great.

34:58.989 --> 35:00.559
Anyway, take a seat.

35:00.560 --> 35:01.560
All right.

35:08.230 --> 35:09.729
Rock never dies!

35:09.730 --> 35:10.770
Hey, what's wrong with my hand?

35:15.339 --> 35:16.369
Do you like metal music too?

35:16.909 --> 35:18.039
Metal, my foot.

35:18.040 --> 35:19.639
Get a grip first.

35:23.150 --> 35:25.650
What about you? Do you like spicy jjamppong?

35:45.069 --> 35:47.000
Oh, is it because of your hair?

35:47.440 --> 35:48.440
Would this help?

35:49.040 --> 35:51.270
Yes, thanks.

36:19.500 --> 36:21.000
(Lee Si Guk)

36:21.139 --> 36:24.210
When I gave you joy, love,

36:24.610 --> 36:26.639
and extra tteokbokki sauce,

36:27.210 --> 36:29.110
you became my regular customer.

36:29.750 --> 36:31.949
Hello, I'm DJ Jun.

36:33.980 --> 36:35.480
(Song requests are welcome.)

36:37.250 --> 36:40.060
(Hanil Bank, 1-year Anniversary of Real Name Financial System)

36:40.889 --> 36:41.889
Gosh.

36:43.630 --> 36:45.089
Hi, Se Gyeong.

36:47.429 --> 36:49.360
Goodness. What's with this guy?

36:49.429 --> 36:52.100
I didn't expect that you'd want to meet me alone.

36:53.739 --> 36:56.908
I didn't expect you'd show up in clothes with the tags still on them.

36:56.909 --> 36:59.440
Hey, thanks for coming. Take a seat.

36:59.569 --> 37:00.639
Okay.

37:04.449 --> 37:05.980
Let me read this story to you.

37:06.310 --> 37:08.218
(Song requests are welcome.)

37:08.219 --> 37:09.618
"There's a girl..."

37:09.619 --> 37:11.650
"who captured my heart without my permission."

37:12.350 --> 37:14.790
"We met seven years ago at a music competition."

37:15.219 --> 37:17.360
"We both won the grand prize as if it were fate."

37:17.790 --> 37:19.860
"However, we couldn't be together at the time."

37:20.259 --> 37:21.859
"I was immature."

37:21.860 --> 37:24.069
"I left to study abroad because I loved piano so much."

37:24.869 --> 37:27.940
"I could only look at her from afar like a fool."

37:28.540 --> 37:31.710
"Now, I'm on my way to meet her."

37:32.009 --> 37:33.080
"Hearing..."

37:33.279 --> 37:37.279
"'100m Before Meeting Her' by Lee Sang Woo..."

37:37.750 --> 37:38.750
"will cheer me up."

37:38.751 --> 37:40.949
Barf. What a lame story.

37:41.080 --> 37:43.949
This story is from Table Seven.

37:45.589 --> 37:46.589
Where is it?

37:52.889 --> 37:53.929
I guess...

37:54.960 --> 37:56.429
you don't remember me.

37:57.400 --> 37:58.469
No.

38:00.170 --> 38:01.540
Do you like spicy tteokbokki?

38:17.989 --> 38:19.049
(Coolis)

38:21.790 --> 38:23.330
Do you want to use this to blot your face?

38:23.429 --> 38:24.759
Yes, thanks.

38:29.500 --> 38:31.568
- Here, thanks.
- It's okay. Just keep it.

38:31.569 --> 38:32.900
Really? Thanks.

38:40.509 --> 38:42.009
(No Se Bum, the cheesy one with glasses)

38:51.049 --> 38:53.790
Oh, this isn't too bad.

38:53.860 --> 38:55.618
Don't be so touched.

38:55.619 --> 38:56.888
I found it on the street on my way here.

38:56.889 --> 38:58.190
That's the lamest thing I've heard.

38:58.589 --> 39:00.559
Gosh, I already can't stand him.

39:00.560 --> 39:02.499
So they call you the Queen of Cello.

39:02.500 --> 39:04.299
I thought you got that nickname because of your face,

39:05.670 --> 39:06.869
but you're quite clever too.

39:06.940 --> 39:07.940
What's he saying?

39:08.900 --> 39:11.339
You said you wanted to see me to give me the photos in person.

39:12.940 --> 39:15.239
That was a good one. You have good taste in men.

39:16.339 --> 39:19.009
I guess I had been looking at you through colored glasses.

39:19.250 --> 39:21.819
You mean, like you're doing now?

39:22.779 --> 39:23.818
Hyun Yul.

39:23.819 --> 39:26.588
I heard the spicy chicken feet dish here was very good.

39:26.589 --> 39:27.589
Try it.

39:28.360 --> 39:31.658
All right. Since you're practically begging me, I shall try it.

39:31.659 --> 39:33.029
But just know this.

39:33.330 --> 39:35.060
I'm not that easy.

39:35.299 --> 39:37.400
Okay. Try it.

39:48.279 --> 39:51.179
Oh, this one has potential.

39:54.679 --> 39:56.350
What's wrong? Is it too spicy?

39:57.290 --> 39:58.420
You can't eat it?

39:59.889 --> 40:01.119
Let me warn you.

40:01.989 --> 40:03.989
If you have a hidden agenda, give up already.

40:04.360 --> 40:05.790
I like older women.

40:05.989 --> 40:07.060
Besides,

40:07.659 --> 40:09.698
I have no interest in stealing my friend's girlfriend.

40:09.699 --> 40:11.130
If I could,

40:11.730 --> 40:14.499
I'd serve in the military for them. That's how much I love them.

40:14.500 --> 40:17.068
My gosh. You mean, you love Yi Chan that much?

40:17.069 --> 40:18.610
No, my older lady friends.

40:19.040 --> 40:20.210
(Bluffer, Kang Hyun Yul)

40:21.710 --> 40:23.509
Are these two the only ones left?

40:24.650 --> 40:27.080
One of them likes men.

40:28.219 --> 40:31.350
So I'm 99 percent sure that it's Ha Yi Chan.

40:31.520 --> 40:33.759
But if it's not him...

40:34.889 --> 40:36.730
Then it means I got this whole thing wrong.

40:37.690 --> 40:39.730
Gosh, that wouldn't be good.

40:42.060 --> 40:43.429
Ha Yi Chan, you got this.

40:44.400 --> 40:46.529
- Here's your soft tofu stew.
- Thank you.

40:47.299 --> 40:48.299
Thank you.

40:48.300 --> 40:49.798
Ladies first.

40:49.799 --> 40:51.739
- Thanks.
- My gosh. Thank you.

40:51.839 --> 40:54.809
Excuse me. Could I get extra chili powder and chili peppers?

40:54.810 --> 40:56.008
- Sure.
- Thank you!

40:56.009 --> 40:57.279
I knew it. It's you.

40:58.449 --> 40:59.509
Here.

40:59.549 --> 41:00.880
Oh, thank you!

41:01.150 --> 41:03.049
- Have a nice day!
- Thank you. Enjoy.

41:03.819 --> 41:05.449
- You'll put the whole thing in?
- Yes.

41:06.619 --> 41:08.159
About this much? That will do.

41:17.400 --> 41:18.400
Oh, my.

41:18.600 --> 41:21.770
My gosh. I don't even see a single drop of sweat.

41:27.679 --> 41:28.880
Se Gyeong, aren't you eating too?

41:29.080 --> 41:31.079
What? Oh, yes. I should eat too.

41:31.080 --> 41:32.350
- Eat up.
- Okay.

41:34.179 --> 41:35.179
Hold on.

41:35.980 --> 41:37.719
Shall I check, just to be sure?

41:38.549 --> 41:41.219
By the way, what happened to your sidekick?

41:41.860 --> 41:42.920
My sidekick?

41:43.089 --> 41:44.659
Your live-in tutor.

41:44.960 --> 41:46.799
He wasn't annoying you today, telling you what to do?

41:47.929 --> 41:49.199
He left.

41:49.299 --> 41:50.929
What? He left?

41:51.270 --> 41:52.799
That do-gooder packed up and left? Why?

41:52.869 --> 41:54.139
I have no idea.

41:54.239 --> 41:56.739
I really can't figure out what upset him.

41:57.940 --> 41:59.940
He lashed out at me and left.

42:00.779 --> 42:02.210
But he has no place to go.

42:04.980 --> 42:06.279
You're worried about him, aren't you?

42:07.449 --> 42:08.480
"Worried?"

42:09.080 --> 42:10.290
Who? Me?

42:10.489 --> 42:11.589
I'm worried about Ha Eun Gyeol?

42:12.889 --> 42:13.889
Why would I worry about him?

42:13.890 --> 42:16.830
I feel like I finally removed something stuck between my teeth.

42:17.830 --> 42:19.029
Try scratching your head.

42:20.000 --> 42:22.429
- My head? Why?
- Just do it. Scratch it.

42:23.630 --> 42:26.839
Oh, I guess he'll be back soon. You're scratching your forehead.

42:27.239 --> 42:28.799
Why? What does this mean?

42:29.000 --> 42:30.339
It's like a biometric navigator.

42:30.569 --> 42:33.269
When you're waiting for someone, your body knows.

42:33.270 --> 42:36.309
Scratching the back of your head means he won't be back for a while.

42:36.310 --> 42:38.580
Scratching the forehead means he'll be back very soon.

42:41.949 --> 42:43.650
Don't worry. He'll be back soon.

42:46.420 --> 42:48.589
Thanks for trying to comfort me.

42:49.719 --> 42:51.489
- Let's eat before it gets cold.
- Okay.

43:02.569 --> 43:04.809
- Gosh, it's so spicy.
- Is it too spicy for you?

43:04.810 --> 43:06.908
- Drink this. This helps.
- It's so spicy.

43:06.909 --> 43:08.080
Drink up.

43:09.080 --> 43:10.679
Hey, you drank from this earlier.

43:11.480 --> 43:13.278
Spit it out. Here.

43:13.279 --> 43:14.850
- Here are some tissues.
- Stop it.

43:15.350 --> 43:16.650
(Ha Eun Gyeol)

43:24.929 --> 43:27.100
I didn't double-check, and it bothers me.

43:29.929 --> 43:30.969
That's right.

43:37.069 --> 43:38.210
(A hopeless slacker)

43:39.139 --> 43:40.239
Here it is.

43:45.250 --> 43:46.549
Oh, here's another one.

43:46.580 --> 43:47.779
(Ha Yi Chan)

43:53.250 --> 43:54.790
(Ha Yi Chan)

43:54.920 --> 43:56.460
Oh, my.

43:59.330 --> 44:01.730
He loves him more than I thought.

44:02.830 --> 44:05.068
I knew it. So it's not you.

44:05.069 --> 44:06.270
(Ha Eun Gyeol)

44:07.000 --> 44:08.540
Do you like me?

44:09.199 --> 44:10.210
Hey.

44:12.610 --> 44:13.980
Be honest with me.

44:16.739 --> 44:18.249
Is it me?

44:18.250 --> 44:20.650
Or is it Yi Chan?

44:27.259 --> 44:28.319
Hey, you.

44:28.989 --> 44:30.159
You're dangerous.

44:30.830 --> 44:32.860
You have a way of making my heart flutter.

44:37.199 --> 44:39.130
My gosh. You're challenging me.

44:40.029 --> 44:41.299
Shall I take this off or not?

44:44.739 --> 44:45.969
Shall I take it off?

44:47.009 --> 44:48.009
Or not?

44:57.449 --> 44:59.088
(Snail Guesthouse)

44:59.089 --> 45:00.089
I'm home.

45:10.130 --> 45:11.799
Hey, Ha Eun Gyeol! Eun Gyeol!

45:12.170 --> 45:13.199
Hey, you.

45:20.239 --> 45:22.580
Hey! You brat.

45:22.810 --> 45:24.979
What about Eun Gyeol? He's not coming back?

45:24.980 --> 45:26.049
Whatever.

45:26.509 --> 45:28.149
If you want him, you go and look for him.

45:28.150 --> 45:30.149
You can't reach him? You don't know where he is?

45:30.150 --> 45:31.449
Will he be back today?

45:31.650 --> 45:34.389
Shoot. I have to do the fitting today.

45:34.560 --> 45:37.059
"Fitting?" What do you mean?

45:37.060 --> 45:38.429
Eun Gyeol didn't tell you?

45:38.630 --> 45:40.758
I agreed to be the judge for his battle...

45:40.759 --> 45:42.060
because he said he'd be my model.

45:42.299 --> 45:44.199
- "Judge for his battle?" - Yes.

45:44.400 --> 45:47.440
They told me to bring a judge if I wanted a battle with them.

45:47.670 --> 45:51.468
Okay, but why are you asking me?

45:51.469 --> 45:53.739
You said Yi Chan got into music because of you.

45:55.009 --> 45:56.638
Well, that's right.

45:56.639 --> 45:59.080
And Yoon Dong Jin became a guitarist thanks to you.

46:00.219 --> 46:03.279
Right. That is true,

46:04.489 --> 46:05.690
but I'm a little busy these days.

46:05.989 --> 46:08.659
As you can see, my presentation is right around the corner,

46:08.819 --> 46:10.589
so I have to finish up my design...

46:10.630 --> 46:12.359
and submit my assignment too.

46:12.360 --> 46:13.699
I'll take care of it for you.

46:14.060 --> 46:15.259
- What?
- Well...

46:15.630 --> 46:17.528
If you have an assignment or need to do research,

46:17.529 --> 46:18.629
or if you need an assistant,

46:18.630 --> 46:19.730
just tell me.

46:19.869 --> 46:23.039
Goodness. Hey. It may seem easy,

46:23.040 --> 46:25.369
but you can't do it unless you're a fashion design major.

46:27.040 --> 46:28.739
This battle has to happen no matter what, Bal San.

46:29.839 --> 46:31.149
I promised Yi Chan that his band...

46:31.150 --> 46:33.009
would be ready to rock and roll before the festival.

46:33.549 --> 46:34.580
So please.

46:35.549 --> 46:37.819
Please help me out.

46:38.719 --> 46:39.719
So?

46:40.489 --> 46:42.758
You said you'd be a judge, and he did your assignment for you?

46:42.759 --> 46:44.529
Hey, get this.

46:44.759 --> 46:46.089
I got an A plus on the assignment...

46:46.630 --> 46:48.529
even though my professor is extremely fussy.

46:49.630 --> 46:50.670
So?

46:52.199 --> 46:54.199
You're going to make him wear this?

46:54.339 --> 46:56.169
- Yes.
- To make people laugh?

46:56.170 --> 46:59.210
No. I want him to be my model at my presentation.

46:59.270 --> 47:00.309
What is this, a penalty?

47:00.310 --> 47:01.979
Have you got a death wish?

47:01.980 --> 47:03.879
Darn you. He's a good-looking guy.

47:03.880 --> 47:06.548
Must you make him wear this hideous outfit? He'll be embarrassed.

47:06.549 --> 47:08.178
Hey, it's a fair deal!

47:08.179 --> 47:09.649
Fair, my foot.

47:09.650 --> 47:10.988
The battle is over now.

47:10.989 --> 47:12.319
So is your deal.

47:12.589 --> 47:14.259
Why do you keep making him do things for free?

47:14.719 --> 47:16.859
Hey, what do you mean he's doing this for free?

47:16.860 --> 47:18.658
I paid him fairly...

47:18.659 --> 47:21.699
for his labor. This is like his part-time job!

47:22.159 --> 47:24.600
"Part-time job?" You paid him fairly?

47:24.799 --> 47:26.170
Hey, didn't you know?

47:26.730 --> 47:28.540
Eun Gyeol took on a side gig at the guesthouse.

47:28.770 --> 47:30.969
What? When?

47:35.710 --> 47:37.549
You know, I heard you helped Bal San...

47:38.049 --> 47:39.580
get an A plus.

47:40.580 --> 47:42.619
Can you help me too?

47:42.880 --> 47:46.289
Oh, that. I had to help him because I had a bit of a situation.

47:46.290 --> 47:48.189
It's just a short essay.

47:48.190 --> 47:49.919
About 8 to 10 pages.

47:49.920 --> 47:52.158
It's part of the course too. I suggest you write it yourself.

47:52.159 --> 47:53.330
You sure know how to negotiate.

47:54.299 --> 47:56.560
Okay. How about a dollar per page?

47:57.029 --> 47:58.029
Deal?

47:59.699 --> 48:01.868
Then I'll write ten pages. Deal?

48:01.869 --> 48:02.900
We have a deal.

48:05.569 --> 48:07.709
Department of Mathematics...

48:07.710 --> 48:09.310
(Essay on Popular Culture)

48:15.850 --> 48:16.880
One moment.

48:20.690 --> 48:22.290
- Jung Young Woo.
- Yes.

48:22.619 --> 48:23.619
Kim Se Young.

48:24.730 --> 48:26.489
- Hong Chang Soo.
- Yes.

48:31.429 --> 48:32.429
Count them and check.

48:51.589 --> 48:53.519
He's that greedy for money?

48:53.520 --> 48:55.559
Hey, who doesn't like money?

48:55.560 --> 48:57.020
I wouldn't call him greedy.

48:57.989 --> 48:59.860
He had his reason.

49:00.159 --> 49:01.159
What was his reason?

49:01.259 --> 49:03.299
I want to buy Yi Chan a guitar.

49:03.529 --> 49:04.569
What?

49:05.770 --> 49:07.669
I already gave him a guitar.

49:07.670 --> 49:10.868
Oh, that. It soaked up moisture, so it doesn't sound so good.

49:10.869 --> 49:14.238
Hey, it's good enough for a mediocre guitarist like him.

49:14.239 --> 49:17.178
Come on, Bal San. A band has to look cool.

49:17.179 --> 49:18.810
We may be broke, but we're cool.

49:18.909 --> 49:21.250
Yi Chan is so lucky.

49:21.650 --> 49:24.449
You're like his lucky charm that suddenly landed in his lap.

49:24.650 --> 49:25.650
You're tutoring him.

49:26.049 --> 49:27.159
You started the band for him...

49:27.420 --> 49:28.560
and want to buy him a guitar.

49:28.659 --> 49:30.929
Why are you so good to him?

49:31.230 --> 49:32.360
Tell me. I want to know.

49:32.960 --> 49:34.330
He said he wanted to twinkle.

49:34.860 --> 49:35.929
What?

49:36.860 --> 49:38.799
He said this could be the last chapter of his youth.

49:39.569 --> 49:41.139
He'll start making money upon graduation.

49:41.869 --> 49:44.239
So before that, he wants to do everything he's ever wanted to do,

49:44.569 --> 49:45.610
which is why...

49:50.139 --> 49:51.779
I want him to shine.

49:54.380 --> 49:55.719
First, on stage.

49:57.420 --> 50:00.119
I nearly burst into tears because I was so touched by his words.

50:01.360 --> 50:03.060
Hey, be good to him.

50:03.460 --> 50:04.630
He's a nice guy.

50:05.759 --> 50:06.960
On top of being multitalented,

50:07.799 --> 50:09.529
he's such a nice, caring person.

50:09.900 --> 50:11.369
Even if he gets home very late, let me know.

50:14.369 --> 50:16.299
Oh, boy.

50:23.739 --> 50:25.250
(Snail Guesthouse)

51:10.319 --> 51:11.730
I want him to shine.

51:12.830 --> 51:14.529
First, on stage.

51:15.659 --> 51:17.159
Then in life.

51:24.069 --> 51:26.270
(Baekwang High School)

51:26.739 --> 51:29.179
First, I want the five-drum set and a large drum right here.

51:29.639 --> 51:31.850
I want Se Gyeong to experience a magnificent performance.

51:31.980 --> 51:33.079
What are you selling?

51:33.080 --> 51:34.449
Don't you need a snake and a pipe too?

51:34.650 --> 51:36.879
Percussion instruments are the only kind of musical instrument...

51:36.880 --> 51:38.690
that can prove that the heart isn't a vestigial organ.

51:39.020 --> 51:40.049
Forget it.

51:40.350 --> 51:42.689
We need two pianos. Here and this spot here.

51:42.690 --> 51:44.759
And we'll use a synth, so pay attention to the sound quality.

51:45.060 --> 51:47.329
Who is Cindy? Why is she performing with us?

51:47.330 --> 51:49.929
A synthesizer, you idiot!

51:50.159 --> 51:51.698
It's a musical instrument, not a person.

51:51.699 --> 51:53.499
It's very expensive.

51:53.500 --> 51:55.169
Gosh, you know nothing about music.

51:55.170 --> 51:56.999
Hyun Yul, is there anything you need to prepare?

51:57.000 --> 51:58.270
What? No, I'm good.

51:58.969 --> 52:01.139
I don't need to impress Se Gyeong.

52:01.380 --> 52:02.810
I'll just flaunt my skills.

52:04.250 --> 52:07.579
Hyun Yul, you're my last hope.

52:07.580 --> 52:10.789
Oh, I have a small wish though.

52:10.790 --> 52:11.790
Okay, what is it?

52:11.791 --> 52:13.349
A solo part with a pin spotlight...

52:13.350 --> 52:15.659
shining down on me and no one else.

52:15.889 --> 52:18.029
That's it. It's about eight minutes long.

52:18.360 --> 52:20.599
- So you want to impress her too!
- So you want to impress her too!

52:20.600 --> 52:21.658
Calm down.

52:21.659 --> 52:22.799
What are you guys doing?

52:24.170 --> 52:25.170
Hey, you're here.

52:26.529 --> 52:28.600
How come you came alone? Where is Eun Gyeol?

52:29.000 --> 52:31.040
Eun Gyeol has gone AWOL.

52:32.210 --> 52:33.839
I can't reach him. He's gone.

52:34.179 --> 52:35.239
- What?
- What?

52:35.509 --> 52:37.009
Eun Gyeol has gone AWOL?

52:37.110 --> 52:38.679
And you haven't heard from him at all?

52:39.409 --> 52:41.179
Does it mean we can't practice today?

52:41.449 --> 52:42.818
That's not important now.

52:42.819 --> 52:45.118
It means we don't even know when and if he'll come back.

52:45.119 --> 52:46.420
He'll come back soon.

52:46.989 --> 52:48.959
Let's practice without him and wait...

52:48.960 --> 52:50.088
Until when?

52:50.089 --> 52:51.729
Until our hair turns gray?

52:51.730 --> 52:54.229
Hey, what if he never comes back? What if he's gone for good?

52:54.230 --> 52:57.159
Darn it. Are you saying we should give up on the performance?

52:58.330 --> 52:59.630
Darn.

53:03.000 --> 53:04.710
Se Gyeong might come.

53:08.880 --> 53:11.310
I wanted to impress Se Gyeong.

53:14.480 --> 53:15.480
Let's swap him out.

53:16.719 --> 53:18.589
- What do you mean?
- Let's get a new guitarist.

53:20.150 --> 53:21.218
What?

53:21.219 --> 53:23.159
I'll bring the guitarist from my choir.

53:23.759 --> 53:25.830
If he starts practicing with us today, he'll catch up in no time.

53:26.429 --> 53:27.959
Yes, let's do that.

53:27.960 --> 53:29.258
That's a very realistic solution.

53:29.259 --> 53:30.969
- Hey!
- You scared me.

53:32.770 --> 53:34.770
You guys are so mean.

53:35.299 --> 53:37.839
Hey, how could you be so heartless?

53:38.339 --> 53:40.839
We pledged to stay together, but our comember has disappeared.

53:41.279 --> 53:42.609
How could you say you'd replace him...

53:42.610 --> 53:44.279
instead of worrying about him first?

53:45.210 --> 53:46.779
Is the band a joke to you guys?

53:47.580 --> 53:50.019
Is it just bait to hook up with girls...

53:50.020 --> 53:51.489
Is the band a joke to you?

53:51.989 --> 53:53.520
Is it just bait to hook up with a girl?

53:55.489 --> 53:57.429
Do you think you have the right to say that to us?

53:58.489 --> 54:00.488
After all, you were the one who kicked out Eun Gyeol!

54:00.489 --> 54:01.859
And you completely ignored him...

54:01.860 --> 54:03.429
to impress Se Gyeong.

54:05.330 --> 54:06.500
Hey, front man.

54:07.299 --> 54:09.600
So what do you want to do?

54:11.009 --> 54:12.040
What?

54:12.409 --> 54:14.179
What's your solution?

54:14.779 --> 54:15.980
Do you even have an alternative?

54:16.179 --> 54:18.110
Have you ever come up with a plan for anything?

54:19.250 --> 54:20.919
If you're our front man,

54:20.920 --> 54:23.419
pick a direction and start paddling already.

54:23.420 --> 54:25.520
We're all about to drown because of you!

54:27.690 --> 54:28.889
We do need to decide.

54:29.790 --> 54:30.790
What should we do?

54:31.130 --> 54:32.629
Shall we find a new member or...

54:32.630 --> 54:33.630
Shut it.

54:34.360 --> 54:36.560
Only Ha Eun Gyeol can be the main guitarist of our band.

54:37.730 --> 54:39.270
I will find him no matter what.

54:39.929 --> 54:41.568
I will find Eun Gyeol at all costs...

54:41.569 --> 54:43.568
and bring him back!

54:43.569 --> 54:45.040
You traitors.

54:51.549 --> 54:53.679
(Name: Ha Eun Gyeol)

54:58.290 --> 54:59.689
(Ha Eun Gyeol, live-in tutor)

54:59.690 --> 55:01.060
(Good-looking, a talented guitarist, smart)

55:02.690 --> 55:03.719
(Name: Ha Eun Gyeol)

55:11.600 --> 55:13.730
(Missing Person)

55:19.210 --> 55:20.368
(Name: Ha Eun Gyeol)

55:20.369 --> 55:21.839
(Who is the bandsman Mom loved?)

55:32.949 --> 55:35.258
Hold on. Come to think of it,

55:35.259 --> 55:37.759
it was because of him that I started pretending...

55:38.089 --> 55:39.630
that I was Mom.

55:40.029 --> 55:41.029
Choi Se Gyeong?

55:44.270 --> 55:46.170
- You are Choi Se Gyeong.
- No, I'm not.

55:48.500 --> 55:49.569
My gosh.

55:51.040 --> 55:52.909
It is you. Don't you know who I am?

55:53.009 --> 55:56.480
Had he not called me by that name that day,

55:57.009 --> 55:59.250
I wouldn't have fallen for...

55:59.909 --> 56:01.349
No, that came out wrong.

56:01.350 --> 56:04.849
Anyway, I wouldn't even have thought to look for Mom's first love.

56:04.850 --> 56:05.888
Also...

56:05.889 --> 56:07.048
You moved to the US without saying goodbye.

56:07.049 --> 56:08.258
You're not supposed to come back,

56:08.259 --> 56:09.919
but you came back, and you're here now.

56:09.920 --> 56:11.889
What is going on?

56:12.730 --> 56:16.428
I got a sense that he knew a lot about Mom.

56:16.429 --> 56:19.929
Something told me that they probably had a very special relationship.

56:20.869 --> 56:21.969
There's only one way.

56:22.239 --> 56:24.909
I must find Ha Eun Gyeol and check it myself.

56:26.969 --> 56:29.210
Please leave a message after the tone.

56:30.210 --> 56:32.179
Hi, Yi Chan! What are you up to?

56:32.449 --> 56:34.380
Can we meet at that cafe at around 7pm?

56:34.619 --> 56:36.079
I'll wait to hear from you.

56:36.080 --> 56:37.850
Page me as soon as you get this message.

56:40.150 --> 56:41.158
Okay.

56:41.159 --> 56:43.020
Please have a look at this. Thank you.

56:43.389 --> 56:45.659
I'm looking for this person. Isn't he handsome?

56:46.060 --> 56:48.758
This tall, good-looking boy is lost...

56:48.759 --> 56:50.868
Hello, I'm looking for someone. Please help me.

56:50.869 --> 56:52.428
I'm looking for this guy.

56:52.429 --> 56:53.968
If you see him, please call me.

56:53.969 --> 56:55.639
Please take this. Thank you.

56:57.770 --> 56:59.069
That rude punk.

56:59.739 --> 57:00.739
Gosh.

57:07.009 --> 57:08.049
Oh!

57:08.380 --> 57:11.449
(Missing Person, Ha Eun Gyeol)

57:20.259 --> 57:22.130
Hello, did you just page me at 0130?

57:22.900 --> 57:24.769
I saw the poster.

57:24.770 --> 57:26.000
You're looking for Ha Eun Gyeol, right?

57:26.830 --> 57:27.940
Yes, that's right.

57:28.339 --> 57:29.540
Do you know where he is now?

57:29.969 --> 57:32.639
Gosh, he'll flip out if he finds out that I told you.

57:33.509 --> 57:35.638
There is a reward though, right?

57:35.639 --> 57:37.210
Yes, for sure.

57:37.339 --> 57:39.480
Where can I meet you?

57:39.679 --> 57:42.179
(Washing Machine, TV, Refrigerator)

57:44.790 --> 57:46.650
This is my fax number.

57:47.150 --> 57:50.190
If something happens, fax me at this number.

57:53.360 --> 57:54.459
(Five Stars Te Amo Fax, 980 Dollars)

57:54.460 --> 57:55.460
(Five Stars Ka Fax, 880 Dollars)

57:55.461 --> 57:56.730
(Daesung Electronics Standard Fax Machine, 1,180 Dollars)

58:28.130 --> 58:31.000
Hey! Watch where you're going!

58:46.150 --> 58:47.179
Hi.

58:48.819 --> 58:49.949
Nice to meet you.

59:00.460 --> 59:01.500
Where is Eun Gyeol?

59:02.630 --> 59:03.759
Where is he now?

59:04.969 --> 59:07.069
How would I know?

59:10.540 --> 59:13.040
Are you naive or dumb?

59:13.369 --> 59:14.880
You're just after money, aren't you?

59:15.040 --> 59:17.310
Bingo.

59:18.480 --> 59:21.079
Now that it's all out in the open,

59:21.080 --> 59:22.420
let's get down to business, okay?

59:22.619 --> 59:24.488
Hand over all the money you have,

59:24.489 --> 59:26.150
and we'll let you go in one piece.

59:26.489 --> 59:27.489
I don't have any money.

59:28.159 --> 59:29.360
Even if I did, I wouldn't give you a penny.

59:30.060 --> 59:32.789
This is the problem with high school kids in this country.

59:32.790 --> 59:35.100
When you're nice to them, they just assume that you're actually nice.

59:38.429 --> 59:41.500
Oh, you're glaring at me.

59:43.369 --> 59:46.069
Guys, what are you waiting for? We don't have time.

59:51.509 --> 59:53.250
- Come on.
- Get up.

01:00:06.790 --> 01:00:08.900
Oh, no. I'm sorry. Are you all right?

01:00:12.400 --> 01:00:14.198
Wait, hold on.

01:00:14.199 --> 01:00:15.699
You can't leave like that!

01:00:18.369 --> 01:00:19.369
Shoot.

01:00:28.080 --> 01:00:31.089
(Ha Yi Chan)

01:00:33.489 --> 01:00:35.420
Yi Chan. Ha Yi Chan.

01:00:35.860 --> 01:00:37.790
Are you all right? Hey, open your eyes.

01:01:42.989 --> 01:01:44.020
Let's do it together.

01:01:45.060 --> 01:01:46.130
The band.

01:01:46.159 --> 01:01:48.230
I will give you the best band as a present.

01:01:48.360 --> 01:01:50.900
I will make your youth twinkle just like your wish.

01:01:52.630 --> 01:01:54.569
Do what I say just this once. Please?

01:01:54.739 --> 01:01:56.199
You just need to be careful this year. Okay?

01:01:58.369 --> 01:02:00.639
I'll keep you safe no matter what.

01:02:00.739 --> 01:02:01.880
Just for a year.

01:02:02.810 --> 01:02:04.679
Just for one year, not your whole life.

01:02:05.279 --> 01:02:07.679
Can't you even stay by my side just for one year?

01:02:30.770 --> 01:02:31.810
Good job.

01:02:33.409 --> 01:02:35.179
I got it. I'll help you then.

01:02:35.339 --> 01:02:36.709
I'll do a band with you.

01:02:36.710 --> 01:02:38.850
I'll teach you how to play guitar. I'll do everything for you.

01:02:41.219 --> 01:02:42.719
Today is our first day together.

01:02:49.020 --> 01:02:50.460
You said you'd keep me safe.

01:02:54.489 --> 01:02:55.860
You said you'd help me get into college...

01:02:57.730 --> 01:02:59.069
and that we should start a band together.

01:03:04.139 --> 01:03:06.509
Ha Eun Gyeol! Where are you, seriously?

01:03:22.420 --> 01:03:26.330
(The Street You Want to Walk, Hongdae Square Stage)

01:03:50.279 --> 01:03:51.718
(Hongdae Real Estate Consulting)

01:03:51.719 --> 01:03:52.989
(Karaoke Music Video Room)

01:03:56.360 --> 01:03:58.329
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

01:03:58.330 --> 01:04:00.230
What year is this?

01:04:01.230 --> 01:04:03.329
It's 2023. Why?

01:04:03.330 --> 01:04:04.699
Did you say 2023?

01:04:05.730 --> 01:04:07.199
Not 1995?

01:04:08.040 --> 01:04:10.238
- What are you talking about?
- Wait.

01:04:10.239 --> 01:04:13.710
Isn't La Vida Music around here? A musical instrument shop.

01:04:14.909 --> 01:04:16.179
No, not that I know of.

01:04:25.750 --> 01:04:26.790
So...

01:04:28.219 --> 01:04:29.489
I've returned to the present?

01:04:57.880 --> 01:05:00.650
(Special thanks to Ryu Jin, Woo Jung Won, and Kim Hae Jun)

01:05:27.980 --> 01:05:32.619
(Twinkling Watermelon)

01:05:32.690 --> 01:05:35.388
Yi Chan didn't come home last night.

01:05:35.389 --> 01:05:38.059
I had a bad dream.

01:05:38.060 --> 01:05:39.629
What about Mom? Where's Mom?

01:05:39.630 --> 01:05:40.928
If you go back now,

01:05:40.929 --> 01:05:43.329
your 2023 will look very different...

01:05:43.330 --> 01:05:45.269
from the 2023 you came from.

01:05:45.270 --> 01:05:46.730
Do you still wish to go back?

01:05:47.029 --> 01:05:48.069
"Yoon Chung Ah?"

01:05:48.239 --> 01:05:49.868
Mom!

01:05:49.869 --> 01:05:51.408
You're not allowed to use sign language in this house.

01:05:51.409 --> 01:05:53.170
What are you doing now?

01:05:53.339 --> 01:05:55.779
I want to help your daughter find the world she lost.

01:05:55.880 --> 01:05:57.079
I want to build her a bridge.

01:05:57.080 --> 01:05:59.710
Yi Chan, it's me. I can't reach you.

01:05:59.980 --> 01:06:01.920
I found Ha Eun Gyeol.
